# Enterprise Sustained License

Version 1.0

## Preamble

Serverless Inc believes in transparency and building in the open. We make our source code available so you can inspect it, learn from it, and contribute to it. Enterprise subscriptions sustain this project and keep it free for everyone else. We're grateful for their support.

**TL;DR:** Free for individuals and organizations under $10M revenue / 100 employees. Large organizations must purchase a subscription. Contributors keep their copyright. Code converts to Apache 2.0 after four years.

## 1. Definitions

"Software" means the Creature application, including all source code, documentation, and associated files made available by Serverless Inc.

"You" or "Your" means the individual or entity exercising rights under this License.

"Organization" means any corporation, limited liability company, partnership, sole proprietorship, non-profit, government agency, or other legal entity.

"Revenue" means the consolidated annual gross revenue of Your Organization and all of its affiliates, subsidiaries, and parent entities, calculated in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles.

"Evaluation Use" means using the Software for evaluation, trialing, proof-of-concept, or training purposes, and expressly excludes Business Purposes.

"Business Purposes" means using the Software for Your Organization's internal operations or to deliver services to clients. Business Purposes expressly excludes Evaluation Use.

"Small Organization" means an Organization with (a) annual Revenue of less than three million United States dollars ($3,000,000 USD), and (b) fewer than twenty-five (25) employees.

"Large Organization" means any Organization that is not a Small Organization.

## 2. Grant of License

**2.1 Free Use.** Subject to the terms of this License, Serverless Inc grants You a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to use, copy, and modify the Software if You are:

(a) A Small Organization, provided You are not using the Software for Business Purposes primarily on behalf of, or for the benefit of, a Large Organization;

(b) An individual using the Software for personal purposes, provided they are not using it on behalf of a Large Organization; or

(c) Any Organization using the Software for Evaluation Use. Evaluation Use should not exceed forty-five (45) days.

**2.2 Paid Use.** Large Organizations using the Software for Business Purposes must purchase a subscription from Serverless Inc.

**2.3 Security Research.** Security researchers may use the Software without restriction for vulnerability research and responsible disclosure.

**2.4 Client Services.** When using the Software to deliver services to a client, the client's qualification under this Section 2 determines licensing requirements. A subscription is required if the client would require a subscription for its own direct use of the Software.

## 3. Honor System

By using the Software, You represent and warrant that Your use qualifies for free use under Section 2.1, or that You have purchased a valid subscription. Serverless Inc trusts You to make this determination honestly and in good faith.

## 4. Restrictions

You may not:

(a) Redistribute, sublicense, sell, or otherwise transfer the Software as a standalone product or service;

(b) Use the Software to create a product or service that competes with the Software;

(c) Remove, alter, or obscure any licensing, copyright, or other proprietary notices contained in the Software; or

(d) Use the Software in any manner that violates applicable law; or

(e) Use the Software, its source code, documentation, or any derivative works to train, fine-tune, or improve machine learning models, artificial intelligence systems, or similar technologies without prior written consent from Serverless Inc.

## 5. Commercial Licensing

The following activities require a separate written agreement with Serverless Inc:

(a) **Reseller Arrangements.** Selling or distributing subscriptions to the Software on behalf of Serverless Inc;

(b) **OEM Licensing.** Embedding, bundling, or integrating the Software into Your own products or services for distribution to third parties; and

(c) **White-Label Licensing.** Rebranding, modifying, or removing Creature branding from the Software for distribution under Your own brand.

To inquire about commercial licensing, contact sales@serverless.com.

